Mark Gouge <Mark_Gouge@compuware.com> wrote:
: I just purchased a DEC Multia Alpha and found that it came with no software.
: After doing some research I have found that it may require the Multia System
: Admin Kit (CD) to access the features of the box.  I plan to run NT 4.0 on
: the box.  Anyone with a copy of the disk that I could buy or use?  This
: machine is no longer in production and not supported by Compaq.  Any help
: will be appreciated.

The Multia System Admin Kit Cd contains NT3.51, not 4.0. However you can
install NT4.0 from the m$ NT install CD.
You just have to switch to the ARC console, then find a menu item: Run
Command, and issue: arcinst. It will partition your HDD. You'll  need a
little FAT partition to boot up NT.

Hope this help

Mihaly



