Kermit 95 doesn't have scrollbars because currently it's a Win32 console
application.  That doesn't mean it doesn't have scrollback -- in fact
it has up to 2000000 lines of scrollback, but it is accessed by other
means (scrollback "verbs" that can be assigned to the keys or mouse
events of your choice; this include line/screen up/down, home/end,
set/goto bookmark, and string search).

The next release of K95 will run in a GUI window and so the scrollback
buffer will also be accessible by scrollbars.  The version upgrade will
be free to registered users of the current version.

