NonStop eBusiness focus sharpened with major re-organization at Compaq Canada
Inc.


    Company now built around Internet Age products, solutions and services

    RICHMOND HILL, ON, Sept. 30 /CNW/ - Compaq Canada Inc. announced today
that, effective immediately, it has re-organized its marketing, sales and
services organizations to align them with the Company's NonStop eBusiness
direction and to meet changing customer requirements.

    The re-organization of the Company is as follows:

    The customer-facing, field sales and services organizations have been
integrated under a Regional Vice President in each of the Company's four sales
territories, while Compaq's channel sales organization will now include both
sales and marketing components. Both sales organizations will continue to
report to one Executive;
Compaq's three services organizations have been amalgamated into two distinct
business groups - Customer Services and Professional Services -- under the
direction of two Executives;
Compaq's product marketing and solutions organizations have been re-engineered
into three distinct business groups - Consumer Products Group, Commercial
Personal Computing Group and Enterprise Solutions & Services Group - under the
leadership of three Executives.
    ``Compaq's value proposition is built around NonStop ebusiness products,
solutions and services - and our Canadian organization must reflect that if we
are to better serve our customers and meet our overall objectives as a
Company,'' explains Peter Ciceri, President & Managing Director, Compaq Canada
Inc. ``For example, I believe the integration of our field sales and services
organizations under the Regional Vice Presidents in each of our four sales
territories will greatly simplify in the mind of the customer who Compaq is
and what value the Company brings to the table as a technology partner.
    ``Similarly, dividing our marketing and solutions organizations into
three distinct business groups reflects the reality that one size does not fit
all - that we market a wide range of products, solutions and services
requiring different approaches and separate business models,'' he adds.
``Finally, the amalgamation of our three service organizations into two
distinct business groups is recognition of the synergies that exist in those
organizations as well as the need to adopt a solutions focus across those
businesses.''
    Ron Hulse, Vice President, Sales, will continue to be responsible for
managing Compaq's overall channel and enterprise sales and pre-sales technical
support activities nation-wide.
    Reporting to him are five Regional Vice Presidents, one who will be
responsible for channel sales and marketing and four who will be responsible
for managing the Company's channel, commercial PC, custom system, enterprise
and partner sales; customer and professional services sales; pre-sales
technical support; and general management activities in their territories.
They are also responsible for customer satisfaction in those geographies.
    Ian Vaudry, formerly Manager, Advanced Technologies, has been appointed
Regional Vice President, Channel Sales & Development. He will be responsible
for managing Compaq's business relationships with its direct and indirect
resellers as well as its OEM (original equipment manufacturer) customers.

    The four Regional Vice Presidents are:

    Andy Canham, Regional Vice President, Western Region, whose territory
includes the provinces of British Columbia, Alberta, Saskatchewan and
Manitoba; Howard Gomes, Regional Vice President, Central Region, whose
territory includes Ontario, except for the National Capital Region (Ottawa);
Larry Higginson, Regional Vice President, Ottawa & Atlantic Canada, whose
territory includes the National Capital Region and the provinces of New
Brunswick, Newfoundland, Nova Scotia and Prince Edward Island; Daniel Mercier,
Regional Vice President, Quebec, whose territory includes the province of
Quebec.
    Derek Smith has been appointed Vice President, Consumer Products Group.
He will be responsible for the overall management of Compaq's consumer PC
business in Canada. This includes marketing responsibility for the consumer PC
product line, sales responsibility for the retail distribution channel and
financial responsibility for the consumer PC business unit. Compaq's consumer
PC products include the marketshare-leading Presario brand of desktop and
notebook PCs and their related options.
    Ralph Hyatt, formerly Vice President, Marketing, and (acting) Vice
President, Consumer Sales & Marketing, has been appointed Vice President,
Commercial Personal Computing Group. He will be responsible for the overall
management of Compaq's commercial PC business in Canada. This includes
marketing responsibility for the commercial PC product line, sales
responsibility for the reseller and distribution channels and financial
responsibility for the commercial PC business unit. Compaq's commercial PC
products include the marketshare-leading Deskpro brand of commercial desktop
PCs, the technology-leading Armada brand of commercial notebook PCs, the
technology-leading Professional Workstation brand of systems, the
innovation-leading Aero brand of handheld PCs, marketshare-leading
Compaq-branded monitors and related PC options.
    Rae Strathdee, formerly Vice President, Customer Services, has been
appointed (acting) Vice President, Enterprise Solutions & Services Group. He
will be responsible for the overall management of Compaq's enterprise
products, enterprise solutions and technology partner relations businesses in
Canada. This includes marketing responsibility for enterprise products and
solutions, sales responsibility for reseller and distribution channels and
financial responsibility for the enterprise products and solutions business
unit. Compaq's enterprise products include the marketshare-leading NonStop
Himalaya and Integrity brands of enterprise systems, marketshare-leading
ProLiant and ProSignia Intel processor-based servers, technology-leading
AlphaServer Alpha 64-bit processor-based servers, marketshare-leading
StorageWorks brand of storage subsystems, innovation-leading Compaq OpenVMS
and Compaq Tru64 UNIX operating systems, industry-leading AltaVista brand
search engine and related enterprise options.
    Reg Schade, formerly Regional Vice President, Channel Sales &
Development, has been appointed Vice President, Customer Services. He will be
responsible for all aspects of the Canadian customer services operations,
including the quality of hardware, software, system management and network
services delivered to more than 10,000 customers. Compaq customer services
include hardware, software and network support, warranty support, and high
availability and NonStop, business-critical support.
    Ron Ratzlaff has been appointed (acting) Vice President, Professional
Services. He will be responsible for managing Compaq's professional services
organization, including sales, practice management, marketing, delivery and
operations. Compaq's professional services include FutureSourcing, the
provision of outsourced networked IT solutions, from the desktop to the
distributed IT enterprise infrastructure; and network and systems integration
services, the planning, design and implementation of IT solutions addressing
mail and NOS migration, application development and integration, ERP
implementation and Internet and network integration.
    Michael Borland, currently Vice President, Legal and General Counsel, has
also been appointed (acting) Vice President, Communications. In addition to
being responsible for providing Compaq with the entire scope of in-house
legal, contract and corporate compliance services, Mr. Borland will also be
responsible for advertising, direct marketing, event marketing and management,
government relations, marketing communications, public relations and user
group relations.

    Other departments within the re-organized Company are as follows:

    Finance & Administration, led by Debbie Young, Vice President, Finance &
Administration, who is responsible for all aspects of Compaq's accounting,
business planning, credit management, financial planning, facilities
management and purchasing.
    Human Resources, led by Daisy Ng, Vice President, Human Resources, who is
responsible for all aspects of Compaq's human resources function, including
human resources strategy and planning, organization effectiveness, development
of organization capabilities, rewards programs, employee engagement and health
and safety.
    Operations, led by Pat Waid, Vice President, Business Operations &
Quality, who is responsible for the functions of business intelligence and
