In article <37EB04BE.71B75F12@rochester.rr.com>, "Trevor R.H. Clarke" <retrev@rochester.rr.com> writes:
:I'm installing NetBSD/vax on a 3100 (M30 I think) and I'm wondering what
:is the latest firmware revision available? I think I've bot v1.3 on
:there but don't quote me on that(I've got so many machine floating around I
:get my numbers crossed sometimes :) ) Can you upgrade w/o VMS or another OS
:installed(like you can with an Alpha 3000?) If so, does someone have
:some images floating around that I can MOP boot to do an upgrade?

  If you have a VAXstation 3100, then you don't have loadable firmware,
  you have a set of PROMs containing the console program and related
  capabilities.  While technically VAX microprocessors of this vintage
  do have something analogous to "firmware", it is etched directly into 
  the VAX microprocessor and is not readily alterable.

  I will assume you are aware of the 1.073 GB limit on the system disk
  capacity, and the availability of OpenVMS hobbyist licenses.  If not, 
  please see the OpenVMS FAQ for further details:

    ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/Digital/dec-faq/OpenVMS.txt

 --------------------------- pure personal opinion ---------------------------
   Hoff (Stephen) Hoffman   OpenVMS Engineering   hoffman#xdelta.zko.dec.com




