Folks,

As a follow-up to Jeff Killeen's posting on DECUS San Diego, here's an
article that appeared in a recent issue of Shannon Knows Compaq. The
election is pretty much a done deal, but DECUS San Diego is only six weeks
off...

DECUS Doings

If you're a member of the DECUS US Chapter, you should have received a
ballot for the 1999 DECUS US Chapter Board of Directors Election. Seven
people--including SKC's publishee--are running for two-year
Director-At-Large positions commencing January 1, 2000. The four candidates
receiving the highest vote counts will be elected to the positions.
Candidate applications are posted on www.decus.org; four candidates also
submitted statements to the Dallas Fort Worth Compaq User Group's Longwords
newsletter.

Please take the time to vote for the candidates of your choice, and be sure
to return your postage-paid ballot so it is received by DECUS before October
1. Thanks for your support!

Moving right along, yet another DECUS US Chapter Symposium is almost upon
us. The Fall 1999 DECUS Symposium will be held at the San Diego Convention
Center in San Diego, CA from November 6 though 11. SKC strongly advises
attendees to submit their registrations and book their hotel rooms ASAP.
Only 1000 rooms have been reserved for this event, hence early bookings are
in the best interest of those who wish to participate in the San Diego
event.

What's on the DECUS San Diego agenda? Compaq CEO Mike Capellas will discuss
the company's enterprise strategy during a keynote address on Monday,
November 8. Sources report that a sneak preview of Compaq's WildFire system
will show up at DECUS as well. Also on tap is a free Storage Days seminar, a
full-day UNIX track, and an address from Mark Menasi, author of The Software
Conspiracy. Conspiracy Theorists also are invited to check out "Compaq's
Strategic Directions," the latest iteration of SKC's Compaq Strategy
presentation. Per usual, the SKC pitch will immediately precede the Compaq
Listens panel discussion.


--
Terry C. Shannon
