I have this nice old MV3100 with Ultrix.  The CD is getting a little
problematic.  Is it possible to build boot tapes from the CD, or
the existing system, or should I be looking for another CD drive?
The machine has a TK50Z drive (don't laugh, I know it is slooooow).
I have made up a set of minimal root and user dump tapes for backup.
Redundancy in booting for emergency recovery seems like a good idea,
considering the age of the machine and its mostly orphan status anymore.
If it were possible to generate bootable tapes, then I could restore
from my dump tapes to have a secondary recovery method available.
I ran across the gentape and genra scripts and was thinking that was
what I was needing, but they called out for kit files to work correctly.
I was going through man pages about kit files, but did not exactly
understand what they were or if they were part of a normal distribution.
Are the details of this covered in the manuals?  I did not find it in
my set, yet.  VAXen and Ultrix are not my forte, and are almost a lost
art form around here, but I would like to learn how it is done, and see
if I can keep the machine running, at least for a while.  It is a nice
plain little unix box.  The only other way I see of maybe keeping a spare
bootable device around is to clone the minimal system drive on a spare
drive.  That seems to have worked OK, but I still like the idea of a
spare bootable tape, just in case.   Any insights of how to make bootable
tapes for the MV3100 series machines is appreciated.

Thanks

Bob




