In article <7sb2u7$asi$1@milo.mcs.anl.gov>,
Tony Scandora 630-252-7541 <scandora@cmt.anl.gov> wrote:
>An old VAX-11/785, mercifully not mine, is running AT&T System V 3.1b UNIX.  It
>is about to be retired for maintenance and Y2K reasons, but it runs useful
>binaries whose sources mignt not be easy to find.
>
>Can one get an updated System V for VAX that is Y2K OK?  Is there any other VAX
>UNIX that will run System V 3.1b binaries?

Though it is unclear whether or not it was officially released, I have
run into people who encountered SVR4 on the VAX in use inside AT&T.  But
I doubt SVR4.2 or subsequent releases ever made it -- so I bet you'd
have trouble getting Y2K patches, and SVR4 was certainly not Y2K
compliant.

It does not do so now, but I'm pretty sure NetBSD/vax could be coerced
fairly easily into running SVR3 binaries -- NetBSD already runs SVR3
(as well as SVR4) binaries on other architectures.  NetBSD is Y2K
compliant, though of course your old binaries may not be no matter
what operating system they're running on.




