I would be surprised if, even though "there was not all that much
to fix", the 5.4 or 5.5 patches are as complete as the 5.7 Y2K
compliance.  Y2K support for Pro380 and 11/93 TOY clocks in SETUP.SAV?
There in 5.7.  Support for both 2-digit and 4-digit-year in IND?
There in 5.7.  Support for 21st century ANSI tape labels?  Yep,
there in both FSM and the utilities.  I think even you'd be surprised
at the nooks and crannies that have to be filled in.

Megan has asked here before, but I too would like to see other folks
make suggestions of what should be done in the next *major*
release, RT-11 6.0, since Mentec/DigiPaq is almost out of tenths :-).
Bring back the SJ monitor?  Support in the kernel for TCP/IP?  Unified
support throughout the OS and CUSPS for partitions larger than
65 kBlocks?  Yep, look in your SSM's, there's been a word reserved
for the cluster factor on every pack, it's just never been used.
Now's the time to ask, everyone!  

