  Ignoring any potential licensing and media right-to-copy issues -- you
  will need to confirm that you have the legal right to copy the media...

  Please see the pointers to discussions of CD-R media in the OpenVMS FAQ 
  as a start...

  Microsoft operating systems are known to corrupt "foreign" storage media 
  via writing "harmless" signatures to media, making "harmless" assumptions
  on the format, and similar activities that will cause you problems in this 
  quest.  Near as I can tell, the entire concept of a "foreign" file system 
  is effectively missing from Microsoft environments...  The CD-R discussions 
  should help you avoid the most common of pitfalls...

