Support for larger disks and partitions sound like a really good idea to me. 
While still possible to find drives under 2Gb, the only easy solution for
getting NEW drives that size are removables such as Zip Drives.  This isn't
a solution I like, as I don't like the reliablity of modern removables.  I
kind of hate wasting large chunks of a drive because the OS can't access
them.  

Of course how well does interfacing the new SCSI Hard Drives with the old 
PDP-11 SCSI adaptors work?  I'm noticing that not only is it getting more
difficult to find small SCSI drives, it's also getting difficult to find
plain 50-pin drives.  Can you use a 68-pin UW SCSI drive with a adaptor?  Of
course now even the UW SCSI drives are becoming less prevalent as the U2W
drives find greater popularity, and the U3W drives are on the way.  But,
none of this is an OS issue :^)

The TCP/IP support would be nice from my point of view, but is it something
that is really needed?  TCP/IP support can be added to RT-11 if needed.

