machines are better engineered than the Venturis, for example, which
looks really cheap and nasty when you open the cover.

This is not to imply a serious criticism of Dec engineering - the Alpha
and Vax range were far better engineered. The BA213 box (for example)
was a marvel of the sheet metal engineers craft. No, I think Dec were
only half serious about the PC market and this is reflected in the
machines they sold.

