respects, but the mini-SCSI connector on the back is a joke, push just
a little bit and it comes loose.  Overall though, a great system.

The latest DEC PCs were in my opinion some of the best, regardless of
mfg, I have seen.  Specifically, the 5510 models, with built in ethernet
and sound.  When required, a modem card is all most ever needed.  While
torx screws are good when required, it is a bit of overkill on a computer
chassis.  The simple thumbscrews on the MicroVAX and the 5510 and 3500
series PCs for removing the cover is slick and as simple as you'd ever
want.  Compaq shut down the DEC PC business just before the rapid advances
in CPU speed, bus speed, and such, but regardless, at that time I feel
that they'd gotten their act together.

