Strav wrote in message <37e17b45.670338@news.naisp.net>...
>A vax we have was recently powered down due to a power problem. It was
>up for about 10 months. Ever since we brought up the vax again, some
>terminals on a decserver appear to "Time out" and logout if a key
>hasn't been hit for 5-10 minutes.
>
>The operator we had is long gone(6 months ago). I think he set
>something to inhibit this from happening.
>
>Anybody have an solution to what to change and how to do it ?

There is a sysgen parameter tty_timeout which is usually set to 900 secs -
but this should only apply to disconnected terminals.

If the decserver was powered off then it would re-load its configuration
from the vax - have a look in sys$sysroot:[decserver]
I think you can set a timeout on each decserver port using something like
>set port 8 timeout 3600
to investigate/fix you will need to use one or more of tsm (terminal server
manager) lcp (lat control program) or ncp (network control program)
Hope this helps
Phil






