darryl heeft geschreven in bericht <937475438.138511@terra.ultra.net.au>...
>Can anyone point me to where the FAQ may be that covers installing3rd
>Party SCSI drives in uVAX200s' ?
>I hooked an IBM 0663 (1 Gig) up and did a T75 which seemed to work.
>When I did a T 76 it gives an error #5.
>Thankx, Darryl Georgee, Australia.
>

The uVAX2000 has no SCSI support. The tapedrive connects to
a bus which looks suspiciously like a SCSI-1 but it only supports
a TK50. Such a TK50 drive however will work on a SCSI bus
(say, on a uVAX3100). If the bus is not that busy an the TK50
at the end, very little device errors appear. I wouldn't recommend
this set up for critical backup purposes...

Hans Vlems





