Mike,

There are a few of these printers still in use. We have had several
discussions about them here in the past. Check the Dejanews archives
first, then see if you have more specific questions. There are also a
couple of former DEC repair techs here that have docs and good
memories.

Yes, you start with a null modem cable, the 25 pin connector is a
standard RS-232 DTE connection. Pressing the "T" button on the back
panel will give you a printout of the configuration and settings. Play
with the dip switch to get the setup you want.

The LN03 uses a subset of ANSI escape codes, while the 'R' model
expects postscript files. There was a temporary page where I got the
control summary for the LN03, but I don't know if it's still
available. He was going to post more of the manuals, but I haven't
looked to see if they are up.

Good luck,
