Beware -- the 730 takes a 30 amp circuit (with associated "appliance"
[round] socket).

I remember when we got our 730 -- we ordered 4.2BSD (just out, at that
time) because we heard that VMS ran so slowly on it (it didn't,
really).  We got it set up and field circus came in to install VMS. 
Wouldn't load, wouldn't load, wouldn't load -- lots of sitting around
staring at the TU58 which didn't move.  Then field circus called HQ,
said "uh-huh" several times, then proceeded to pull the card cage out to
reveal the *real* boot TU58 inside.  Installation proceeded apace from
this point...

I remember hacking the 4.2BSD RL02 driver.  It had been written to retry
on errors, but the retry count had been set to zero.  Ah, memories...



