Malcolm Dunnett (dunnett@mala.bc.ca) wrote:
:    Perhaps that's something they had to add to support the DS10.

:    I know that Tru64 Unix supports the IDE CD-ROM on the DS10 ( just
: installed one ), I would imagine the latest VMS does also.

Nope, IDE CD-ROMs were already supported on PWS au-series under DU 4.0d -
quite some time before DS10 came out. This is done by using a translation 
layer between regular SCSI driver and ATA controller, so that IDE CD-ROMs 
appear as SCSI CD-ROMs sitting on very small (max 2 devices) SCSI chain. 
Although CD-ROMs are all that is supported officially, I had also seen 
reports of people using IDE hard drives under DU on au-series boxes - 
with rather horrible performance, though.

Since SOC lists identical base hardware configuration (which includes
IDE CD-ROM) for both DU and VMS au-series, I presume these CD-ROMs are 
also useable under VMS.

