Once upon a time, I was a Product Engineer in Kanata for the MicorVAX 3100
Model 10 and 20 and InforServer Model 100, 150 and 1000.

The InfoServer 100 is in fact a fully functional MicroVax 3100 Model 20,
with different PROM's. Yes, MicroVax memory cards fit and you will enjoy a
better caching performance. As I remeber the old InfoServer software, it
self tuned on the extra memory, but look at all the parameters in the latest
version, you may have some flexibility for tweaking.

The InfoServer 150 was a MicroVAX Model 10e with different PROM's yet again
and the FPU chip was never installed from what I remember, so no conversion
to anything here. This was a reduced cost unit with two externally available
SCSI ports to make life more interesting.

The InfoServer 1000, was a CVAX chip with a SIM and a Network Chip of modest
performance. This was really a cost concious unit and extremely focused in
design, compared to the first two units based on already built hardware and
metal.

Considering how long the product has been EOL, I am always quite happy to
see them at work and hear about them, still giving reliable service after
all these years.

