Hi,

I have two RZ29L disks I would like to install in a StorageWorks
cabinet. Problem is they make the system hang on heavy disk
access. All SCSI termination has been checked, and I have come to the
conclusion that the problem arises because these disks are fast SCSI
disks (no other units on the SCSI chain are fast SCSI).

To overcome the problem I would like either to configure the SCSI
adapter (AHA1742A) to limit transfer speeds to 5MB/s, or to install a
second adapter to have the disks on a separate (shorter) SCSI chain in
a second disk cabinet.

Unlike the ECU for PC systems, the ECU 1.11A for Digital Unix does not
support overlay (.OVL) files. The Adaptec AHA1740 Enhanced Mode
configuration is in an overlay file, and there is no replacement for
this on the Digital Unix ECU. Is it possible to configure the maximum
transfer rate by any other means?

I also tried to install a second AHA1742A (removing the floppy jumper
J6), however after configuring with the ECU the boot procedure
eventually fails with
"aha_process_intr: spurious interrupt on ctlr 0x0".
The first card is using IRQ 11, and the second IRQ 12. I believe I
read somewhere that the cards are supposed to share IRQ 11, but the
ECU won't allow this.

Does anybody out there have a solution to my problems?


Best regards,

Dag



