: Tim Llewellyn wrote:
: > One real sad computer collector I encountered wanted a 730
: > because apparently its all TTL, no custom chips so you can fix it
: > with a scope and a Maplins catalogue :-)

Me, by any chance?

The VAX11/730 is one of the only 2 families of VAXen I'd want to have to 
maintain (the other being the 11/780, of course) for exactly this reason. 
The 11/730 CPU is 3 hex cards of simple PALs, AMD bit-slice (2901 ALUs, 
etc) and other common chips. There are 2 gate arrays in there for memory 
error correction, but I believe there are ways to kludge over those if 
they ever fail.

Fitting a complete VAX onto 1.5* the board area of a PDP11/34 using only 
standard chips was (IMHO) quite a hack.

-tony




