michael@gladia.astro.rug.nl writes:
> Are they just bipolar proms?  Can someone point me to
> an outfit who will blow one to order.  Preferably in
> the UK, but not essential.  Thanks in advance.

  You don't say what card you're trying to fix. On the older DEC cards,
there was a ROM with the address in it. On newer DEC cards, as well as
most 3rd-party cards, it's part of the configuration data EEPROM on the
main Ethernet chip, and while it's programmable, the information on how
to do so (and the related tools) are generally not available to end
users.

