You have to get a hold of CD #1 from the Consolidated Software Distribution
("Jan 1993" or "Mar 1993"). There will be save sets in the root directory of
the form VMS055.A -> VMS055.F (I think) along with mandatory patches
VMSMUP55.A -> VMSMUP55.D (I think). The "dash two" update will be of the
form VMSU2055.A -> VMSU2055.D (I think). The reason I'm going through all
this is that I have seen many factory pre-gened VAX's installed with VMS 5.5
but the software delivered to the same site also contained the "dash two"
upgrade which never got installed. Check your site. You may already have the
upgrade save sets on the shelf. If you still need to get the upgrade you
might wish to poke around http://www.openvms.digital.com

ps. If at all possible, consider upgrading to VMS 6.2 since it seems to
manage memory quite a bit better.

