This happens to me when ever the leader of the self threading tape breaks
off. If you're careful this can be done on a running system depending on the
mounting configuration. If rack mounted, then unscrew and remove the front
plate. Reach in behind and unplug the flat data cable. Unscrew the thumb
screws that retain the TK70 and slide it out until the power plug (a white
molex connector) can be seen and unplugged. Now slide out the tape drive and
take it to a work bench where you'll have to take it apart so that you can
unlock the handle that ejects the cartridge.

