Too bad, looks like you have a Windows NT only machine. The HWPRB, Hardware
Restart Parameter Block is created by the SROM (Serial Read Only Memory)
that brings up the system on power up. If your SROM does not do this, then
you have a Windows NT only machine. Both UNIX and OpenVMS require a valid
HWPRB to be able to identify the CPU/System type and also to find good
memory and to be able to start up the system. For more info on the HWPRB,
read the VMS Internals book.

DO NOT CONFUSE SRM and SROM, these are two different things.


rtt





