Firstly, on an alpha, the BIOS is stored in flash, with various
parameters being stored in an NVRAM. Neither of these bears any
resemblance to an EPROM, and an EEPROM (which I also doubt they use
much) isn't erased by UV light.

Even if you did find a chip which you could erase, you would only be
destroying your system, since you have no way of reprogramming
whatever it was you just wiped.

I can only ask at this point whether you're *extremely* malicious, or
merely naive and ignorant.
 
