Hi Jim,

TZ885 has several operation modes which are controlled via the
key switch on the front.
There is an "automatic" which has to be used when your software
is able to control a loader, like for instance Legato does.
If you do not have the privilege of having one of these tools,
you use the "round-robin" mode. In this case you have to insert
the first tape manually, with the buttons on the front. After that
you can do your backup with some unix tool. When finished the
tape has to be unmounted in a way that it is ejected from the drive.
The changer will then put the cartridge in its slot and insert the next
one into the drive. If the cartridge from the last slot was used the
changers moves over to slot 1 again.
So this way, your software does NOT even have to know about
the changer, as long it is able to eject the tape.

If you want to have more specific info about the changer, please email
me, maybe i can check it out.

cheers
Robert Schmoelzer
Telemed Communications Services, Austria
