In article <7raogk$3t7$1@nnrp1.deja.com>, Jim Bews <j.r.bews@st-and.ac.uk> 
>
> [ The customer is trying to use a TZ885 with vdump... ]

>Any help for someone who is a complete novice on alphas and autochangers
>would be much appreciated.

This is easy.  Vdump doesn't support sequential media changers.  I
was lead to believe that it might have been modified at one point
to send the necessary offline command, but if it is prompting for
the next the feature is nearly useless for unattended backups.

There are two solutions:

1.  Get a real backup package that provides full media changer
    support; Networker for example.

2.  Use expect to run the vdump program and let it handle the
    answer to the prompt.  I've never done this, but I've
    read of people that have.  Going this route will allow
    you to use MRU to do random access where convient.

