    Well I am not.  The complex logic built into the comm link hub/memory
    controller/cache snoop port to insure coherence must be the proverbial
    heart of darkness. To get it right and convince yourself it is correct
    under all possible conditions is not a minor feat; it probably makes
    the '264 core seem simple in comparison.

    Think of how many processors (not to mention chipsets) have run into
    trouble with errors in their initial implementation of SMP cache
    coherency with just one system bus to worry about (R4000MC, Xenon,
    PPC620 and many more).  The EV7's magic box has to worry about four
    high speed com links, two levels of on-chip cache, and a honking
    great memory controller with god knows how many read and write ports
    and buffers etc.

