CPU Lockstepping is the technique used by Tandem systems to provide fault
tolerance, so that the working CPU will be in the identical state to the CPU of
the failed half-system, and therefore able to take over for it.

When integrated circuits are designed, the data file(s) that contain the
information are (or were) often written to tape for transfer to the fabrication
facility.  Hence, "taped out" means that the design phase (of at least this
cycle of design-test-fix) is finished.

                                RDP

