Yep, the 21464 "Arana" will implement symmetric multithreading (SMT).
And the 21364 *is* essentially a '264 core with the added bells and
whistles mentioned above. The onboard memory and I/O controllers and
comms links will enable the 21364 to dispense with core logic chipsets
(such as Tsunami and Typhoon in the DS20 and ES40), hence the "glueless
SMP" sobriquet.

According to the Q, the 21364 will in fact incorporate the hardware
necessary for CPU lockstepping. That's why Tandem can/will base its
future Himalaya boxes on EV7 rather than waiting for EV8.

