I think you have to be a little careful about the wording of the press
release.  What they said is 

	"It's simply the fastest desktop computer ever, easily running
	up to a stunning 100% to 200% faster than the fastest Pentium
	III-based PCs"

I would say that most people consider DESKTOP machines to be PC's and
Mac's (as well as other minor machines - amiga, acorns etc).  The Alpha
machines, while the fit on the desktop, are generally considered
Workstations or Servers, not desktop machines.

It is still quite fast.  A 450-500MHz machine has a sustained throughput
of about 1gigaflop and a peak of about 4gigaflops.  This puts it in the
league of a single Vector processor from Figitsu and other such super
computers.  

