JF Mezei (jfmezei.spamnot@videotron.ca) wrote:
> How come Compaq doesn't challenge publicly Apple for the title of the fastest
> chip ? Does Compaq know it has Alpha which is the fastest chip in  the world 
> and it is its duty to defend its title ?

I think it's the duty of the entire RISC segment to challenge the
Xeon/NT/SQL supremacy on the TPC-C benchmark for 4-cpu systems (and
soon, 8-cpu systems), but that's not happening either.

I think the rule these days is 'if you can find ONE thing your chip
does faster than any other chip, you can claim to be the fastest chip
in the world'.  Apparently, the PowerPC camp used an old Byte benchmark
to make such a claim in the past, and may be doing so again.

The G4-PPC with Altivec is a really interesting CPU, and the Apple
systems should make interesting Linux boxes.  I see a lot more volume
on the comp.os.linux.powerpc news group vs. the comp.os.linux.alpha
news group.  It could be that the days of the Alpha being the coolest
Linux box are numbered.  I don't seem to see much in the way of
affordable 21264 systems, but once you let Apple do their early product
cycle price gouging the G4-PPCs should be a great enthusiast class
product with excellent availability.  The 'leaked' Enrico P. memo spoke
of a Linux push for Alpha, but words are cheap.

