Sorry - that was at least partially facetious.  Some of the snapshot support
already out there (though not, I believe, NetApp's) works at the virtual
disk level (e.g., EMC's and StorageTek/IBM RAMAC's, I think), so it
potentially *could* be useful in VMS environments.  The main difficulty with
such low-level snapshots is coordinating them with higher-level activity
such that they catch a (transactionally, logically) consistent image at that
higher level - especially if you try to do so without requiring a lengthy
quiescence at that higher level.

- bill

