Gamberufo Gatto wrote:
> 
> This afternoon I passed by a salvage yard and came away with a PRO 380
> and two CIPHER SCSI tapes (new, still in the original package).
> 
> Unfortunately the PRO 380 didn't have a video or keyboard. At home
> I cleaned it all up and then fired it; the disk is a RD52-A and it
> seems to boot some OS because I can hear the heads seeking. Nothing
> comes out on the comm1 port and 3 out of 4 LEDS on the back a lit
> (except number 3). I didn't find any explanations about the LEDS
> in the PRO FAQ on update.uu.se.
> 
> Being curious about the OS on the disk I pulled id out and tried to
> hook it up un my PDP 11/73. The disk was jumpered in DS1 but my 11/73
> docs say to jumper DS3. With both jumperings the 11 always complains
> that the disk is not ready.

The low-level format that a RQDX[1,2,3] expects and that the
PRO hard disk controller expects are radically different.

> Is there some additional trick to make the disk the disk visible?

If you want to interchange information between the PRO and your
11/73, you'll have to come up with a different way.  If you
want to reformat the drive and use it on your 11/73, all you have
to do is run the ZRQC?? formatter from your XXDP diagnostic set.

Tim.



