That isn't the point. the 4 way ES40 is slower than 4 way Xeon boxes
though to be fair they are using SQL-Server on NT and the ES40
is using Sybase on Tru64 so the results are not directly comparable.

Even the 8 CPU 6/700 GS140 results only come in ~3% better than
an 8 CPU Xeon, though again SQL-Server was used fro the Xeons.

>
> The Sun Enterprise 450 is about 30% behind the ES40 in TPC-C.  Just a
> little figure in the interest of fairness.
>

Yes I know, but its hardly relevant in a discussion about the Aphas
ability to compete with Intel as an NT platform. To my knowledge
no one markets NT on SPARC so the Sun E450 is hardly relevant.

But just as a question. Why would you be happy that the ES40 is
30% faster than a Sun E450, they are both 4 CPU machines
but the E450 CPUS are according to Rob half the speed ?

Though both systems used Sybase the ES40 used Sybase 11.9.3
with the Sun E450 using 11.5. On Sun at least 11.9.3 is faster
and in some cases a lot faster than 11.5. Care to speculate
how much of the 30% was caused by using a faster version of
Sybase ?

The ES40 is ~40% more expensive per transaction than
the E450, doesn't have the applications portfolio that the
Sun does, its physically bigger while supporting less internal
storage etc etc etc.


