A. Khan wrote in message <7qmtek$dsj$2@news6.svr.pol.co.uk>...
>Hi...many thx to those who responded to my post for help with a lead...
>
>I now have a cable which has 25 pins female on one end and 25 pins male on
>the other, and a "Null modem adapter" with 25 pin female on both ends...
>
>1) Will this leadage work for a PC?

It depends on if the serial port on your PC was configured correctly.  It
should be a male 25 pin wired DTE.  However I have seen more than a few that
were wired DCE through internal jumpers.

The 25 pin FEMALE connector on the back of your PC is a parrallel connector.
It will not work to drive the LN03.

>2) Where on earth/has anyone got a driver to get this printer working with
>windows 98??


You may have to just use GENERIC TEXT, if an LN03 or ANSI printer is not in
the list.
Also check to see if anything is at http://www.windows.digital.com.

>(An emailed response would be much appreciated:))


Ask here, get something resembling an answer here.


-John





