		-- Athlon/Williamette providing much better IA32 performance
		   and cheaper.

		-- OSes not nearly ready for Merced this time next year.

		-- Lack of applications.

	The one bright spot Intel holds out and the darling of IDF is
	Linux.  However, Alpha boxes have a good solid year to come down
	in price with UP1000 MotherBoards and to ramp all the way to
	1.5 GHz according to recent comp.arch post.  Lot of work to
	do to really push Alpha Linux and box prices too.  If that UP1000
	could drop an Alpha down to < $2000 with modest memory, etc.
	it could almost be a Merced shutout as that UP1000 and an 800 MHz
	21264 should be equivalent to Merced in performance and much 
	cheaper.

	I wouldn't be surprised after Intel has their day to see a great
	Alpha Linux campaign to begin in a week or so.  Wouldn't be 
	surprised at all.  Just a feeling.

