>   on these is not generally available.  (These protocols are not specific
>   to the Q-bus nor to Q-bus controllers.)

  I though we did this at least once before 8-)

  A censored version of the MSCP specs was published by DEC. It excludes the
sections on host support for controller-initiated bad block replacement as
well as the section on the enhanced functions implemented on HSC's. It also
wasn't revised when the "real" version was revised (so, for example, it says
that unit numbers only go up to 255, not 4095).

  The part number is QP906-GZ, the description is "DSA CONTROLLERS V1.0 DOC
KIT", the lead time is 7 days, and the price is $107. There is also QP905-GZ,
"UDA50 PROG V1.0 DOC KIT-ARCHI", 7 days, $74. The "ARCHI" in the description
is probably "ARCHIVED" - both of these doc kits are in maintenance mode as
DEC no longer makes new MSCP stuff. When I ordered these a number of years
ago, DEC asked me if photocopies were acceptable, but that was before they
went to Kodak on-demand printing for low-volume documents.

