Greetings.

I'm writing because I would like to acquire a dirt-cheap (used) Alpha-
based PC and because I could use pointers and/or offers.

I want an Alpha-based PC for the following reasons:
     + To use to learn about OpenVMS & Alpha hardware.
       (I currently possess an infinitesimal amount of knowledge about

       both.)
     + To use to learn about FreeBSD (and possibly Linux).


Now that you know my motives, perhaps you can recommend an Alpha-based

PC that would be suitable and that would also meet the following 
criteria: 
    1. Capable of running the hobbyist version of OpenVMS and the 
       general version of FreeBSD without ANY difficulty.
    2. VGA support. (Being able to use an IBM keyboard would be nice 
       too; is that a standard Alpha feature?
    3. Support for off-the-shelf commodity HDs of 2GB or more. (It 
       doesn't actually have to have one of that size, but it should 
       support it).
    4. CDROM capable; Serial & Parallel port equipped.
    5. Available cheaply ($100 - $300).
(Again, if you have a computer meeting the above criteria -- with 
documentation! -- that is just gathering dust, perhaps you might want 
to consider parting with it?)

While becoming familiar with Alphas, I've accumulated a few questions.

Care to give'em a try? If the answers are posted somewhere, do accept 
my apologies for wasting your time and do, please, point me there!
    a. What sort of expansion bus do Alphas have? Do they support 
       commodity ISA or other IBMish cards? I'd imagine they wouldn't 
       support IBMish cards with installed firmware, due to the 
       difference in CPU's, but what about dumb cards like serial 
       adapters (for example)?
    b. What sort of documentation is available for Alphas, how is it 
       acquired, and for how much? Does DEC also produce technical 
       reference/service manuals and are they affordably priced?
    c. While spying on you chaps, I've occasionally read of $1.5k 
       Alpha PC's they were superior to IBM PC's. Of the very few 
       places I've been able to locate that sell Alphas, none sell 
       anything like that. Though there is no possibility of my 
       purchasing such a computer in the near future, I'd be 
       interested to know if such a beast exists and where it is sold.
    d. Do I really have much of a chance of setting up an Alpha to 
       boot OpenVMS AND FreeBSD via a partitioned hard drive? Care to 
       point me to any useful web sites/postings/etc.?

In conclusion, thanks for reading this far and for any help you might 
be able to offer.


Cordially,
Richard Kanarek

